{comment: 12-bar blues in G: G G G G, C C G G, D7 C G G. Swing the eighths (long-short).}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
Oh, [G]have you heard the latest,
The latest of the songs?
It's a[C]bout that little boll weevil,
Picked [G]up both feet and gone,
A-lookin' for a [D7]home, a-[C]lookin' for a [G]home. [D7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
The [G]farmer took the boll weevil
And put him in hot sand.
The [C]weevil said, "This is mighty hot,
But I'll [G]stand it like a man;
This'll be my [D7]home, this'll [C]be my [G]home." [D7]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
The [G]farmer took the boll weevil
And put him on the ice.
The [C]weevil said to the farmer,
"This is [G]mighty cool and nice;
This'll be my [D7]home, this'll [C]be my [G]home." [D7]
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: G}
